@host = http://localhost:8080
@contentType = application/json

# Search for works inside one reading source, through whichever provider serves it.
# The response is { providerKey, results: [{ externalId, title, url }] }: providerKey is the provider that
# ran the search, and each externalId is only valid for it. externalId and url are null when the site
# doesn't give them in a search listing (Suwayomi results carry no public url).
#
# Needs the backend running, the reading sources already synced (see sync.http) and, for Suwayomi sources,
# a Suwayomi Server with the site's extension installed.

### Login as the admin seeded by data.sql (any authenticated user can search)
# @name login
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "usernameOrEmail": "admin",
  "password": "admin",
  "rememberMe": false
}

### Sync if needed
# @name firstSync
POST {{host}}/api/moderation/reading-sources/sync
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.access_token}}

### List - approved sources, to pick the id to search in
GET {{host}}/api/reading-sources?statuses=APPROVED&sortBy=NAME&direction=ASC

### Search - in one source -> 200
# Copy the id of the source to search in from the list above.
@sourceId = 10
# @name search
GET {{host}}/api/reading-sources/{{sourceId}}/search?keywords=pick me up
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.access_token}}

### Search - no Authorization header -> 401
GET {{host}}/api/reading-sources/{{sourceId}}/search?keywords=pick me up

### Search - blank keywords -> 400
GET {{host}}/api/reading-sources/{{sourceId}}/search?keywords=%20
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.access_token}}

### Search - missing keywords -> 400
GET {{host}}/api/reading-sources/{{sourceId}}/search
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.access_token}}

### Search - unknown source -> 404 (ComicReadingSourceNotFoundException)
GET {{host}}/api/reading-sources/999999/search?keywords=pick me up
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.access_token}}

### Search - source not approved -> 409 (ComicReadingSourceNotApprovedException)
# Needs a PENDING source: propose one with a new source from the submit flow (see reading-entries.http),
# then put its id here.
@pendingSourceId = REPLACE_ME
GET {{host}}/api/reading-sources/{{pendingSourceId}}/search?keywords=pick me up
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.access_token}}


# ─── Details of one search result, on demand: what a search listing doesn't carry (chapters, url...) ───
# Asks the provider that ran the search for that work, without saving anything. Each call reaches the
# remote site, so it is meant to be made when the user opens a result, not for every result.

### Details of the first result of the search above -> 200 { title, url, availableChapters, latestChapterAt }
GET {{host}}/api/reading-sources/{{sourceId}}/search-result-details?providerKey={{search.response.body.$.providerKey}}&externalId={{search.response.body.$.results[0].externalId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.access_token}}

### Details - no Authorization header -> 401
GET {{host}}/api/reading-sources/{{sourceId}}/search-result-details?providerKey={{search.response.body.$.providerKey}}&externalId={{search.response.body.$.results[0].externalId}}

### Details - a work that doesn't exist for that provider -> 400 (comic-not-found-in-reading-source) or 502 if it can't tell
GET {{host}}/api/reading-sources/{{sourceId}}/search-result-details?providerKey={{search.response.body.$.providerKey}}&externalId=999999999
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.access_token}}

# ─── Create the entry from a search result: no url needed, the provider that ran the search hydrates it ───

### Import a comic to attach the entry to (Pick Me Up)
# @name importComic
POST {{host}}/api/catalog/myanimelist/154587
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

### Create an entry from the first result of the search above -> 201, hydrated (title, chapters, url)
# The request carries the providerKey of the search, because the externalId is only valid for that provider.
# If the provider can't hydrate the work the entry is NOT created (502, or 400 if the work no longer exists).
POST {{host}}/api/comics/{{importComic.response.body.$.slug}}/reading-entries/from-search-result
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.access_token}}

{
  "sourceId": {{sourceId}},
  "providerKey": "{{search.response.body.$.providerKey}}",
  "externalId": "{{search.response.body.$.results[0].externalId}}",
  "locale": "en"
}

### Create an entry from a search result - same work again -> 409 (DuplicateComicReadingEntryException)
POST {{host}}/api/comics/{{importComic.response.body.$.slug}}/reading-entries/from-search-result
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.access_token}}

{
  "sourceId": {{sourceId}},
  "providerKey": "{{search.response.body.$.providerKey}}",
  "externalId": "{{search.response.body.$.results[0].externalId}}",
  "locale": "en"
}

### Create an entry from a search result - a providerKey that serves no such source -> 400 (reading-source-not-supported)
POST {{host}}/api/comics/{{importComic.response.body.$.slug}}/reading-entries/from-search-result
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.access_token}}

{
  "sourceId": {{sourceId}},
  "providerKey": "does-not-exist",
  "externalId": "1",
  "locale": "en"
}

### Create an entry from a search result - no Authorization header -> 401
POST {{host}}/api/comics/{{importComic.response.body.$.slug}}/reading-entries/from-search-result
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "sourceId": {{sourceId}},
  "providerKey": "{{search.response.body.$.providerKey}}",
  "externalId": "{{search.response.body.$.results[0].externalId}}",
  "locale": "en"
}
